# 04 — Domain Adapters

## 1. The v1 Problem

In v1, FDM and FEM rendering were forked **inside** the renderer:
- `UnifiedViewport3D` had a `discretization` prop
- Layer components checked `discretization` to decide rendering strategy
- The `Viewport3DModel` in `view3d/contracts.ts` knew about both FDM and FEM fields

This means every new rendering feature had to be implemented twice, and the "unified" viewport was unified in name only.

## 2. v2 Strategy: Adapter Pattern

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  FDM_API["FDM grid data"] --> FdmAdapter["FdmDomainAdapter"]
  FEM_API["FEM topology binary"] --> FemAdapter["FemDomainAdapter"]
  FdmAdapter --> RenderModel["TopologyRenderData"]
  FemAdapter --> RenderModel
  RenderModel --> Renderer["MeshLayerRenderer"]
```

The renderer sees only `TopologyRenderData`. It doesn't know if the data came from a structured grid or an unstructured mesh.

## 3. Interface — lives in `src/domain/adapters/`

```typescript
export interface SpatialDomainAdapter {
  readonly kind: "fdm" | "fem";
  readonly generationId: number;
  readonly pointCount: number;

  getBounds(): Bounds3;
  getPositions(): Float32Array;
  getIndices(): Uint32Array | null;
  getNormals(): Float32Array | null;
  getRenderGeometry(): RenderGeometry;
  getDomainInfo(): DomainInfo;
}
```

This interface is reused from v1 (`apps/web/src/domain/adapters/SpatialDomainAdapter.ts`) but promoted to `src/domain/adapters/` in the control-room.

## 4. FDM Adapter

FDM domains have structured grids — no explicit topology.

```typescript
export class FdmDomainAdapter implements SpatialDomainAdapter {
  readonly kind = "fdm";

  constructor(private meta: DomainMeta) { ... }

  getPositions(): Float32Array {
    // Build cell-center positions from grid shape + origin + spacing
    const [nx, ny, nz] = grid.shape;
    const [ox, oy, oz] = grid.origin;
    const [dx, dy, dz] = grid.spacing;
    // ... interleaved xyz
  }

  getIndices(): Uint32Array | null {
    return null; // FDM: no explicit topology
  }

  getRenderGeometry(): RenderGeometry {
    return {
      positions: this.getPositions(),
      indices: null,  // renderer uses instanced cubes
      normals: null,
      cellCount: this.pointCount,
      vertexCount: this.pointCount,
    };
  }
}
```

**FDM rendering note:** MeshLayerRenderer detects `indices === null` and uses `THREE.InstancedMesh` with cube geometry at cell centers. The cube size comes from grid spacing.

## 5. FEM Adapter

FEM domains have unstructured meshes with explicit topology (boundary faces).

```typescript
export class FemDomainAdapter implements SpatialDomainAdapter {
  readonly kind = "fem";

  constructor(private meta: DomainMeta, private topology: DecodedTopology) { ... }

  getPositions(): Float32Array { /* from topology.positions */ }
  getIndices(): Uint32Array | null { return this.topology.boundaryFaces; }
  getNormals(): Float32Array | null { return this.computeNormals(); }

  getRenderGeometry(): RenderGeometry {
    return {
      positions: this.getPositions(),
      indices: this.topology.boundaryFaces,
      normals: this.computeNormals(),
      cellCount: this.topology.elementCount,
      vertexCount: this.pointCount,
    };
  }
}
```

## 6. Render Model Builder

Pure function: takes adapter output + resource data → `Viewport3DRenderModel`.

```typescript
export function buildViewport3DRenderModel(
  adapter: SpatialDomainAdapter | null,
  field: FieldResourceSnapshot | null,
  visualization: VisualizationState,
  selection: SelectionState,
): Viewport3DRenderModel {
  if (!adapter) {
    return EMPTY_RENDER_MODEL;
  }

  const geometry = adapter.getRenderGeometry();

  return {
    topology: {
      positions: geometry.positions,
      indices: geometry.indices,
      normals: geometry.normals,
      cellCount: geometry.cellCount,
      vertexCount: geometry.vertexCount,
      topologyRevision: adapter.generationId,
      domainKind: adapter.kind,
    },
    scalarField: field ? mapScalarField(field, visualization) : null,
    vectorField: field ? mapVectorField(field, visualization) : null,
    layers: visualization.layerVisibility,
    selection: mapSelection(selection),
    displayMode: visualization.displayMode,
    // ...
  };
}
```

## 7. Resource Hooks

These hooks live in `src/modules/viewport-3d/hooks/useViewport3DResources.ts` and aggregate multiple resource hooks into a single snapshot:

```typescript
export function useViewport3DResources(kernel: KernelApi) {
  const sessionStatus = useSessionStatus(kernel);
  const revisions = sessionStatus?.revisions;

  const meshTopology = useMeshTopology(kernel, revisions?.topology);
  const fieldData = useFieldData(kernel, revisions?.field, activeQuantity);
  const vizState = useVisualizationState(kernel);

  const adapter = useMemo(() => {
    if (!sessionStatus?.domain) return null;
    return createDomainAdapter(sessionStatus.domain, meshTopology?.decoded);
  }, [sessionStatus?.domain, meshTopology]);

  return { adapter, fieldData, vizState };
}
```

## 8. Field Resource Hook

```typescript
export function useFieldData(
  kernel: KernelApi,
  fieldRevision: number | undefined,
  quantityId: string | null,
) {
  // Only refetch when fieldRevision changes
  // Decode binary field data via codec
  // Return typed arrays for scalar and vector components
}
```

**Critical:** field refetch does not trigger topology refetch. They are independent resources with independent revision pointers.

## 9. File Locations

```
src/domain/
  adapters/
    SpatialDomainAdapter.ts        # interface (ported from v1)
    FdmDomainAdapter.ts            # FDM: structured grid
    FemDomainAdapter.ts            # FEM: unstructured mesh
    createDomainAdapter.ts         # factory function
  render-models/
    meshRenderModel.ts             # TopologyRenderData type
    fieldRenderModel.ts            # ScalarFieldRenderData, VectorFieldRenderData
    sliceRenderModel.ts            # for 2D viewport (later)
  units/
    coordinates.ts                 # SI unit normalization
    quantities.ts                  # quantity metadata
```
